  "narrative": {
    "intro": "V3GATE has $672M in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. V3GATE won 514 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $1.3M. Obligations fell 18.3% year over year. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer of V3GATE services, obligating $389M so far in FY2026. Other major agency buyers include the Department of State ($59.7M), the Department of Homeland Security ($56.2M), and the Department of Defense ($29.2M). The single largest market for V3GATE is Other Computer Related Services, which accounts for $668M in obligations. Historical obligations show a peak in FY25 of $822M, with FY26 at $672M year to date and earlier years at $711M (FY24), $648M (FY23), $387M (FY22), and $371M (FY21). Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date obligations. Award-value and contract-value distinctions follow standard reporting: obligations are shown for current totals and award-value figures appear in other award tables when noted.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are V3GATE's biggest customers?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is V3GATE's largest customer, obligating $389M in FY2026 to date. The Department of State and the Department of Homeland Security follow with $59.7M and $56.2M respectively. The Department of Defense obligated $29.2M and the Department of Justice obligated $28.5M. Several other civilian agencies each obligate between $9.7M and $22.5M, including Transportation ($22.5M), Energy ($16.9M), Social Security Administration ($14M), Treasury ($10.6M), and Labor ($9.7M)."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and contract sizes drive V3GATE's business?",
        "body": "Other Computer Related Services is V3GATE's dominant market, accounting for $668M in obligations in FY2026 to date. Custom Computer Programming Services accounts for $2.8M and Electronic Computer Manufacturing accounts for $632K. V3GATE has 514 awards this fiscal year with an average award size of $1.3M, and total obligations of $672M year to date."
      }
    ]
  },
